# What the hold walk asks of the code around a fact: whether a statement's impure calls can reach a list the task holds
# (`reaches-lists`), change a list's length (`keeps-lengths`, `only-keeps-lengths`), or only push (`body-only-pushes`);
# which list a statement pushes to or pops from; whether a body leaves a turn early or writes through a member; which
# values are scalars and which locals only ever hold one; what a write forgets (`forget-writes`); and the closures an
# expression builds, whose holds are checked on their own.
#
# Each of these was a reflective walk in the original, over `unknown`: a stack of whatever it was handed, popped last
# first, descending every field but `type`, `span` and `binding`, and never visiting one object twice. Here each is a
# typed walk over node handles: `node-children` (compile/node-children.tree) is the descent the original's default made,
# in the same order, and a handle's node is remembered by the host's identity, so a node two parents share is still met
# once. Popped from the same end, the handles come out in the order the original's objects did.
#
# Ported from check/holds.ts (self-hosting, 2026-10-06), part four. The decisions:
#   - the walk's sets are hashes of flags, and a set the original left out (`fresh`, `params`, `constants`, `scalars`)
#     is an empty hash, which every test the original made of it answers the same way
#   - check/purity.tree answers what is impure, what a subtree writes and what it reads, as check/facts.ts handed it
#   - the tally a caller owns is `hold-tally`, converted by the face both ways: the original created its `seen` and its
#     `kinds` the first time it counted, so the record says whether they exist

load @term/base/list
  find list
  find get

load @term/base/maybe
  find maybe

load @term/base/text
  find split
  find starts-with

load ../parser/diagnostic
  find diagnostic

load ../compile/node
  find expression
  find statement
  find function-param
  find hold-origin
  find type
  find expression-type
  find statement-span

load ../compile/node-children
  find node-handle
  find node-children
  find block-handles

load ./certificate
  find inequality

load ./inequality
  find to-linear
  find constant-of

load ./nonlinear
  find plain-path

load ./universal
  find hold-calls

load ./hold-facts
  find forget
  find drop-fields
  find drop-element-paths
  find without-state
  find mentions-atom
  find is-state-atom
  find key-root
  find has-text
  find add-text

load ./hold-state
  find hold-state

load ./purity
  find subtree
  find calls-impure
  find written-names
  find root-name
  find immutable-kinds
  find read-only-list-methods
  find everything
  find only-statement

# ---- the walk ----

# how many obligations of one tier-0 kind, and how many proven
form kind-count
  mark shared
  link total, like number
  link proven, like number

# one tier-0 obligation that was not proven: the task, what it was owed for, its ordinal among that task's of that kind
form failed-obligation
  link task, like text
  link origin, like hold-origin
  link ordinal, like number
  link diagnostic, like diagnostic

# the tier-0 count of one compile, as the caller's `Tally`: `seen` and `kinds` exist once something was counted
form hold-tally
  mark shared
  link total, like number
  link proven, like number
  link failed, like list, like failed-obligation
  link has-seen, like boolean
  link seen, like hash, like text, like number
  link has-kinds, like boolean
  link kinds, like hash, like text, like kind-count

# what a walk needs besides its facts: where to report, which tasks are pure, which names the task binds itself, which
# names a closure may write behind the walk's back, and what the whole program says of the rest
form hold-walk
  link diagnostics, like list, like diagnostic
  link file, like text
  link pure, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link functions, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link local, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link volatile, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link origin-only, like boolean
  link tally, like maybe, like hold-tally
  link task, like maybe, like text
  link globals, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link state-free, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link keeping, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link fresh, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link returning, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link params, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link constants, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link scalars, like hash, like text, like boolean

# ---- identity ----

# a set of nodes by identity, which the original's `seen` was
bind fresh-seen
  like unknown
  case node
    text <new Set()>
  case browser
    text <new Set()>
  case rust
    text <std::rc::Rc::new(()) as std::rc::Rc\<dyn std::any::Any\>>
  case swift
    text <(NSMutableSet() as Any)>
  case kotlin
    text <(java.util.IdentityHashMap\<Any, Boolean\>() as Any)>

# is this the first time the handle's node is met: remembered if so
bind seen-first
  take seen, like unknown
  take handle, like node-handle
  like boolean
  case node
    text <($seen.has($handle.node) ? false : ($seen.add($handle.node), true))>
  case browser
    text <($seen.has($handle.node) ? false : ($seen.add($handle.node), true))>
  case rust
    text <true>
  case swift
    text <true>
  case kotlin
    text <true>

# ---- small makers ----

task handles
  like list, like node-handle

  back make list

task texts
  like list, like text
  mark private

  back make list

task flags
  like hash, like text, like boolean

  back make hash

task skip-plain
  like list, like text

  save out, texts()
  push(out, <type>)
  push(out, <span>)
  push(out, <binding>)
  back out

task skip-places
  like list, like text
  mark private

  save out, texts()
  push(out, <type>)
  push(out, <span>)
  back out

task expression-handle-of
  take e, like expression
  like node-handle

  back
    make node-handle/expression-handle
      bind node, e

task statement-handle-of
  take s, like statement
  like node-handle

  back
    make node-handle/statement-handle
      bind node, s

task expression-handles
  take items, like list, like expression
  like list, like node-handle

  save out, handles()
  walk items
    take item
    push(out, expression-handle-of(item))
  back out

# the parts check/purity.tree reads, of what the original handed a name walk
task block-parts
  take body, like list, like statement
  like list, like subtree

  save out, make list
  save one
    make subtree/in-block
      bind node, body
  push(out, one)
  back out

task statement-parts
  take s, like statement
  like list, like subtree

  save out, make list
  save one
    make subtree/in-statement
      bind node, s
  push(out, one)
  back out

task expression-parts
  take e, like expression
  like list, like subtree

  save out, make list
  save one
    make subtree/in-expression
      bind node, e
  push(out, one)
  back out

task handle-parts
  take handle, like node-handle
  like list, like subtree

  sift handle
    case expression-handle
      back expression-parts(node)
    case statement-handle
      back statement-parts(node)
    miss
      back make list

# does a subtree call something impure, by the walk's sets
task impure-in
  take parts, like list, like subtree
  take walk, like hold-walk
  like boolean

  save is-pure
    task
      take name, like text
      like boolean
      back walk/pure/has(name)
  save is-function
    task
      take name, like text
      like boolean
      back walk/functions/has(name)
  save is-local
    task
      take name, like text
      like boolean
      back walk/local/has(name)
  back calls-impure(parts, is-pure, is-function, is-local)

# a call as the original's `{ ...call, args: [] }`: the callee alone judged
bind without-arguments
  take call, like expression
  like expression
  case node
    text <(\{ ...$call, args: [] \})>
  case browser
    text <(\{ ...$call, args: [] \})>
  case rust
    text <$call>
  case swift
    text <$call>
  case kotlin
    text <$call>

task callee-impure
  take call, like expression
  take walk, like hold-walk
  like boolean
  mark private

  back impure-in(expression-parts(without-arguments(call)), walk)

task written-in-block
  take body, like list, like statement
  like list, like text

  back written-names(block-parts(body))

task root-of
  take target, like expression
  like maybe, like text

  back root-name(target)

# ---- types ----

# the kind of a node's type, `''` when it has none
task kind-of
  take given, like maybe, like type
  like text

  sift given
    case some
      link known
      back known/kind
    case none
      back <>

# the kind of a list type's element, `''` when it is not a list
task element-kind-of
  take given, like maybe, like type
  like text
  mark private

  sift given
    case some
      link known
      sift known
        case array
          back element/kind
        miss
          back <>
    case none
      back <>

task scalar-kinds
  like list, like text

  save out, texts()
  push(out, <number>)
  push(out, <float>)
  push(out, <boolean>)
  push(out, <string>)
  push(out, <unit>)
  push(out, <bytes>)
  back out

task is-scalar-kind
  take kind, like text
  like boolean

  back has-text(scalar-kinds(), kind)

task is-array-typed
  take e, like expression
  like boolean

  back is-equal(kind-of(expression-type(e)), <array>)

# `/^[0-9]+$/`
bind digits-only
  take value, like text
  like boolean
  case node
    text </^[0-9]+$/.test($value)>
  case browser
    text </^[0-9]+$/.test($value)>
  case rust
    text <(!$value.is_empty() && $value.chars().all(|c| c.is_ascii_digit()))>
  case swift
    text <(!$value.isEmpty && $value.allSatisfy(\{ $0.isASCII && $0.isNumber \}))>
  case kotlin
    text <($value.isNotEmpty() && $value.all \{ it in '0'..'9' \})>

task has-index
  take e, like expression
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift e
    case member
      link member-target
      link member-name
      link member-index
      sift member-index
        case some
          link at
          back true
        case none
          back false
    miss
      back false

# ---- scalars ----

# a list whose elements are scalars
task scalar-list
  take target, like expression
  like boolean
  mark private

  back and(is-array-typed(target), is-scalar-kind(element-kind-of(expression-type(target))))

# does an expression carry no reference to a Term value: its type is a scalar, it reads one element out of a list of
# scalars, or it reads a local that only ever holds such values
task scalar-value
  take e, like expression
  take locals, like hash, like text, like boolean
  like boolean

  fork test, is-scalar-kind(kind-of(expression-type(e)))
    hold
      back true
  sift e
    case variable
      link variable-name
      fork test, locals/has(variable-name)
        hold
          back true
    miss
      save nothing, 0
  sift e
    case binary
      link op
      link left
      link right
      back and(scalar-value(left, locals), scalar-value(right, locals))
    case integer
      back true
    case boolean
      back true
    case string
      back true
    case member
      link member-target
      link member-name
      link member-index
      save positional, digits-only(member-name)
      sift member-index
        case some
          link at
          save positional, true
        case none
          save nothing, 0
      fork test, positional
        hold
          back scalar-list(member-target)
      back false
    case call
      link callee
      sift callee
        case member
          link callee-target
          link callee-name
          fork test, or(is-equal(callee-name, <get>), is-equal(callee-name, <at>))
            hold
              back scalar-list(callee-target)
          back false
        miss
          back false
    miss
      back false

task value-table
  like hash, like text, like list, like expression
  mark private

  back make hash

task push-value
  take values, like hash, like text, like list, like expression
  take name, like text
  take value, like expression
  mark private

  fork test, not(values/has(name))
    hold
      save fresh, make list
      save values/{name}, fresh
  save held, values/get(name)
  push(held, value)

# The locals of a task that only ever hold scalars: every binding of the name, and every plain assignment to it, is a
# scalar value given the others, a fixed point from "all of them" down
task scalar-locals
  take body, like list, like statement
  take params, like list, like function-param
  like hash, like text, like boolean

  save values, value-table()
  save order, texts()
  save disqualified, texts()
  save stack, block-handles(body)
  save seen, fresh-seen()
  walk test
    hook test, is-above(stack/length, 0)
    hook hold
      save handle, stack/pop()
      fork test, not(seen-first(seen, handle))
        hold
          turn next
      sift handle
        case statement-handle
          sift node
            case let
              link let-name
              link init
              add-text(order, let-name)
              push-value(values, let-name, init)
            case assign
              link target
              link op
              link value
              sift target
                case variable
                  link target-name
                  add-text(order, target-name)
                  push-value(values, target-name, value)
                miss
                  save nothing, 0
            case for-each
              link item
              add-text(disqualified, item)
            case function
              link task-name
              link fn-params
              link fn-body
              walk written-in-block(fn-body)
                take name
                add-text(disqualified, name)
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        case expression-handle
          sift node
            case closure
              link closure-params
              link closure-body
              walk written-in-block(closure-body)
                take name
                add-text(disqualified, name)
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
      walk node-children(handle, skip-plain())
        take child
        push(stack, child)
  walk params
    take param
    fork test, not(is-scalar-kind(kind-of(param/type)))
      hold
        add-text(disqualified, param/name)
  save scalars, flags()
  walk order
    take name
    fork test, not(has-text(disqualified, name))
      hold
        save scalars/{name}, true
  save changed, true
  walk test
    hook test, changed
    hook hold
      save changed, false
      walk order
        take name
        fork test, not(scalars/has(name))
          hold
            turn next
        save every, true
        walk values/get(name)
          take value
          fork test, not(scalar-value(value, scalars))
            hold
              save every, false
              halt
        fork test, not(every)
          hold
            scalars/remove(name)
            save changed, true
  back scalars

# ---- what impure calls reach ----

# a call that changes no list's length: `xs/get i` or `xs/at i` on a list, `xs/set i, v`, a method on a value no method
# can change handed only such values, or a task that only ever does such things
task keeps-lengths
  take call, like expression
  take walk, like hold-walk
  like boolean

  sift call
    case call
      link callee
      link args
      sift callee
        case variable
          link callee-name
          back and(walk/functions/has(callee-name), walk/keeping/has(callee-name))
        case member
          link callee-target
          link callee-name
          link callee-index
          save immutable, immutable-kinds()
          fork test, has-text(immutable, kind-of(expression-type(callee-target)))
            hold
              save every, true
              walk args
                take a
                fork test, not(has-text(immutable, kind-of(expression-type(a))))
                  hold
                    save every, false
                    halt
              fork test, every
                hold
                  back true
          sift callee-index
            case some
              link at
              back false
            case none
              save nothing, 0
          fork test, not(is-array-typed(callee-target))
            hold
              back false
          fork test, and(or(is-equal(callee-name, <get>), is-equal(callee-name, <at>)), is-equal(args/length, 1))
            hold
              back true
          back and(is-equal(callee-name, <set>), is-equal(args/length, 2))
        miss
          back false
    miss
      back false

task reads-a-list
  take callee, like expression
  take args, like list, like expression
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift callee
    case member
      link callee-target
      link callee-name
      link callee-index
      sift callee-index
        case some
          link at
          back false
        case none
          save nothing, 0
      fork test, not(has-text(read-only-list-methods(), callee-name))
        hold
          back false
      fork test, not(is-array-typed(callee-target))
        hold
          back false
      walk args
        take a
        fork test, not(is-scalar-kind(kind-of(expression-type(a))))
          hold
            back false
      back true
    miss
      back false

# could an impure call in these nodes reach a list the task holds? Only through what it is handed, a method called on
# a value, or a function value. So an impure call to a TASK OF THE PROGRAM handed only scalars reaches no local list,
# and native code handed only scalars holds no Term value
task reaches-lists
  take start, like list, like node-handle
  take walk, like hold-walk
  like boolean

  save stack, handles()
  walk start
    take one
    push(stack, one)
  save seen, fresh-seen()
  walk test
    hook test, is-above(stack/length, 0)
    hook hold
      save handle, stack/pop()
      fork test, not(seen-first(seen, handle))
        hold
          turn next
      sift handle
        case expression-handle
          save call, node
          sift call
            case call
              link callee
              link args
              fork test, callee-impure(call, walk)
                hold
                  save scalars, true
                  walk args
                    take a
                    fork test, not(scalar-value(a, walk/scalars))
                      hold
                        save scalars, false
                        halt
                  save on-module, false
                  sift callee
                    case member
                      sift root-of(callee)
                        case some
                          link root
                          save on-module, and(and(not(walk/local/has(root)), not(walk/globals/has(root))), not(walk/functions/has(root)))
                        case none
                          save nothing, 0
                    miss
                      save nothing, 0
                  fork test, or(reads-a-list(callee, args), keeps-lengths(call, walk))
                    hold
                      save nothing, 0
                    miss
                      save program-task, false
                      save callee-name, <>
                      sift callee
                        case variable
                          link name
                          save callee-name, name
                          save program-task, walk/functions/has(name)
                        miss
                          save nothing, 0
                      fork test, program-task
                        hold
                          fork test, not(and(walk/state-free/has(callee-name), scalars))
                            hold
                              back true
                        miss
                          fork test, not(and(on-module, scalars))
                            hold
                              back true
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
      walk node-children(handle, skip-plain())
        take child
        push(stack, child)
  back false

# does every impure call in these nodes change no length, with none passing a function value on. With `besides-fresh`,
# a push onto a name bound only to fresh lists is allowed too
task only-keeps-lengths
  take start, like list, like node-handle
  take walk, like hold-walk
  take besides-fresh, like boolean
  like boolean

  save stack, handles()
  walk start
    take one
    push(stack, one)
  save seen, fresh-seen()
  walk test
    hook test, is-above(stack/length, 0)
    hook hold
      save handle, stack/pop()
      fork test, not(seen-first(seen, handle))
        hold
          turn next
      sift handle
        case statement-handle
          sift node
            case function
              back false
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        case expression-handle
          save call, node
          sift call
            case closure
              back false
            case variable
              link name
              fork test, and(walk/functions/has(name), not(walk/pure/has(name)))
                hold
                  back false
            case call
              link callee
              link args
              save fresh-push, false
              fork test, besides-fresh
                hold
                  sift callee
                    case member
                      link callee-target
                      link callee-name
                      link callee-index
                      sift callee-index
                        case none
                          fork test, is-equal(callee-name, <push>)
                            hold
                              sift callee-target
                                case variable
                                  link target-name
                                  save fresh-push, and(is-array-typed(callee-target), walk/fresh/has(target-name))
                                miss
                                  save nothing, 0
                        case some
                          link at
                          save nothing, 0
                    miss
                      save nothing, 0
              save read-only, false
              sift callee
                case member
                  link callee-target
                  link callee-name
                  link callee-index
                  sift callee-index
                    case none
                      save read-only, and(has-text(read-only-list-methods(), callee-name), is-array-typed(callee-target))
                    case some
                      link at
                      save nothing, 0
                miss
                  save nothing, 0
              fork test, and(and(callee-impure(call, walk), not(keeps-lengths(call, walk))), and(not(fresh-push), not(read-only)))
                hold
                  back false
              # the callee itself was judged; only the arguments are left to look at, and a method's receiver
              walk args
                take a
                push(stack, expression-handle-of(a))
              sift callee
                case member
                  link callee-target
                  push(stack, expression-handle-of(callee-target))
                miss
                  save nothing, 0
              turn next
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
      walk node-children(handle, skip-plain())
        take child
        push(stack, child)
  back true

# ---- pushes and pops ----

# the tasks that ARE a list's push: the whole body is `send back, call p/push v` with p and v the task's own two
# parameters in order
task list-pushes-of
  take program, like list, like statement
  like hash, like text, like boolean

  save out, flags()
  walk program
    take s
    sift s
      case function
        link task-name
        link params
        fork test, is-unequal(params/length, 2)
          hold
            turn next
        sift only-return(s)
          case some
            link value
            sift value
              case call
                link callee
                link args
                sift callee
                  case member
                    link callee-target
                    link callee-name
                    fork test, and(is-equal(callee-name, <push>), is-equal(args/length, 1))
                      hold
                        fork test, and(names-variable(callee-target, get(params, 0)/name), names-variable(get(args, 0), get(params, 1)/name))
                          hold
                            save out/{task-name}, true
                  miss
                    save nothing, 0
              miss
                save nothing, 0
          case none
            save nothing, 0
      miss
        save nothing, 0
  back out

# the tasks that ARE a list's pop: the whole body is `send back, call p/pop` on the task's only parameter
task list-pops-of
  take program, like list, like statement
  like hash, like text, like boolean

  save out, flags()
  walk program
    take s
    sift s
      case function
        link task-name
        link params
        fork test, is-unequal(params/length, 1)
          hold
            turn next
        sift only-return(s)
          case some
            link value
            sift value
              case call
                link callee
                link args
                sift callee
                  case member
                    link callee-target
                    link callee-name
                    fork test, and(and(is-equal(callee-name, <pop>), is-equal(args/length, 0)), names-variable(callee-target, get(params, 0)/name))
                      hold
                        save out/{task-name}, true
                  miss
                    save nothing, 0
              miss
                save nothing, 0
          case none
            save nothing, 0
      miss
        save nothing, 0
  back out

# the value a task's one statement sends back, when that statement is a `send back`
task only-return
  take s, like statement
  like maybe, like expression
  mark private

  sift only-statement(s)
    case some
      link only
      sift only
        case return
          link value
          back value
        miss
          back make none
    case none
      back make none

task names-variable
  take e, like expression
  take name, like text
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift e
    case variable
      link variable-name
      back is-equal(variable-name, name)
    miss
      back false

# the path a statement pops one item off: `call p/pop` or the list method `call pop, p`, alone or as the value of a
# binding, with `p` a plain path to a list
task popped-path
  take statement, like statement
  take pops, like hash, like text, like boolean
  like maybe, like text

  save value-read, statement-value(statement)
  sift value-read
    case some
      link value
      sift value
        case call
          link callee
          link args
          sift callee
            case member
              link callee-target
              link callee-name
              link callee-index
              sift callee-index
                case none
                  fork test, and(is-equal(callee-name, <pop>), is-equal(args/length, 0))
                    hold
                      back listed-path(callee-target)
                case some
                  link at
                  save nothing, 0
            case variable
              link callee-name
              fork test, and(pops/has(callee-name), is-equal(args/length, 1))
                hold
                  back listed-path(get(args, 0))
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
    case none
      save nothing, 0
  back make none

task listed-path
  take list, like expression
  like maybe, like text
  mark private

  fork test, is-array-typed(list)
    hold
      back plain-path(list)
  back make none

# the value of an expression statement, a binding, or a plain assignment to a name
task statement-value
  take statement, like statement
  like maybe, like expression
  mark private

  sift statement
    case expression
      link expr
      back make(some, expr)
    case let
      link let-name
      link init
      back make(some, init)
    case assign
      link target
      link op
      link value
      sift target
        case variable
          back make(some, value)
        miss
          back make none
    miss
      back make none

# the path a statement pushes one item onto, when it is exactly `call p/push, <value>` with `p` a plain path to a list
# and the value reaching no list, or the list method `push(xs, v)`
task pushed-path
  take state, like hold-state
  take statement, like statement
  take walk, like hold-walk
  take pushes, like hash, like text, like boolean
  like maybe, like text

  sift statement
    case expression
      link expr
      sift expr
        case call
          link callee
          link args
          sift callee
            case variable
              link callee-name
              fork test, and(pushes/has(callee-name), is-equal(args/length, 2))
                hold
                  save list, get(args, 0)
                  fork test, is-array-typed(list)
                    hold
                      save pushed, handles()
                      push(pushed, expression-handle-of(get(args, 1)))
                      fork test, not(reaches-lists(pushed, walk))
                        hold
                          back plain-path(list)
              back make none
            case member
              link callee-target
              link callee-name
              link callee-index
              sift callee-index
                case some
                  link at
                  back make none
                case none
                  save nothing, 0
              fork test, or(is-unequal(callee-name, <push>), not(is-array-typed(callee-target)))
                hold
                  back make none
              fork test, is-unequal(args/length, 1)
                hold
                  back make none
              fork test, reaches-lists(expression-handles(args), walk)
                hold
                  back make none
              back plain-path(callee-target)
            miss
              back make none
        miss
          back make none
    miss
      back make none

# the plain paths every `p/push v` in a body pushes to, nested walks and branches included
task push-targets
  take state, like hold-state
  take body, like list, like statement
  take walk, like hold-walk
  take pushes, like hash, like text, like boolean
  like list, like text

  save out, texts()
  save stack, block-handles(body)
  save seen, fresh-seen()
  walk test
    hook test, is-above(stack/length, 0)
    hook hold
      save handle, stack/pop()
      fork test, not(seen-first(seen, handle))
        hold
          turn next
      sift handle
        case statement-handle
          sift node
            case expression
              sift pushed-path(state, node, walk, pushes)
                case some
                  link target
                  add-text(out, target)
                case none
                  save nothing, 0
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
      walk node-children(handle, skip-plain())
        take child
        push(stack, child)
  back out

# how a loop body changes state: the number of `p/push v` statements when those are its ONLY changes a local list could
# see, or -1 when it makes any other impure call that may reach one. A closure's body counts, because it may run here
task body-only-pushes
  take state, like hold-state
  take body, like list, like statement
  take walk, like hold-walk
  take pushes, like hash, like text, like boolean
  like number

  save count, 0
  save stack, block-handles(body)
  save seen, fresh-seen()
  walk test
    hook test, is-above(stack/length, 0)
    hook hold
      save handle, stack/pop()
      fork test, not(seen-first(seen, handle))
        hold
          turn next
      sift handle
        case statement-handle
          sift node
            case expression
              sift pushed-path(state, node, walk, pushes)
                case some
                  link target
                  save count, add(count, 1)
                  turn next
                case none
                  save nothing, 0
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        case expression-handle
          sift node
            case call
              save start, handles()
              push(start, handle)
              fork test, reaches-lists(start, walk)
                hold
                  back -1
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
      walk node-children(handle, skip-plain())
        take child
        push(stack, child)
  back count

# does a body write through a member anywhere, a closure's body included
task writes-through-member
  take body, like list, like statement
  like boolean

  save stack, block-handles(body)
  save seen, fresh-seen()
  walk test
    hook test, is-above(stack/length, 0)
    hook hold
      save handle, stack/pop()
      fork test, not(seen-first(seen, handle))
        hold
          turn next
      sift handle
        case statement-handle
          sift node
            case assign
              link target
              sift target
                case member
                  back true
                miss
                  save nothing, 0
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
      walk node-children(handle, skip-plain())
        take child
        push(stack, child)
  back false

# does a body leave a turn before its end, anywhere in it (a nested walk's own `halt` included, conservatively), a
# closure's or a nested task's body excepted
task exits-early
  take body, like list, like statement
  like boolean

  save stack, block-handles(body)
  save seen, fresh-seen()
  walk test
    hook test, is-above(stack/length, 0)
    hook hold
      save handle, stack/pop()
      fork test, not(seen-first(seen, handle))
        hold
          turn next
      sift handle
        case statement-handle
          sift node
            case function
              turn next
            case break
              back true
            case continue
              back true
            case return
              back true
            case throw
              back true
            case exit
              back true
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        case expression-handle
          sift node
            case closure
              turn next
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
      walk node-children(handle, skip-plain())
        take child
        push(stack, child)
  back false

# a walk whose only change to state is pushes with pure arguments, from a condition or sequence that calls nothing
# impure: keepAcrossTurns has already kept exactly the length facts such a walk preserves
task only-pushing-loop
  take state, like hold-state
  take statement, like statement
  take walk, like hold-walk
  take pushes, like hash, like text, like boolean
  like boolean

  sift statement
    case while
      link cond
      link body
      fork test, impure-in(expression-parts(cond), walk)
        hold
          back false
      fork test, is-below(body-only-pushes(state, body, walk, pushes), 0)
        hold
          back false
      back not(writes-through-member(body))
    case for-each
      link item
      link index
      link iterable
      link body
      fork test, impure-in(expression-parts(iterable), walk)
        hold
          back false
      fork test, is-below(body-only-pushes(state, body, walk, pushes), 0)
        hold
          back false
      back not(writes-through-member(body))
    miss
      back false

# what a statement's (or expression's) impure calls leave of the facts: a call that changes no length and no field
# leaves all but what was known through a list position. Any other impure call may change any state, except that one
# which cannot reach a LOCAL list leaves local lengths alone
task impure-effect
  take state, like hold-state
  take current, like list, like inequality
  take start, like list, like node-handle
  take parts, like list, like subtree
  take walk, like hold-walk
  take pushes, like hash, like text, like boolean
  like list, like inequality

  fork test, not(impure-in(parts, walk))
    hold
      back current
  fork test, only-keeps-lengths(start, walk, false)
    hold
      back drop-element-paths(current)
  fork test, is-equal(start/length, 1)
    hold
      sift get(start, 0)
        case statement-handle
          fork test, only-pushing-loop(state, node, walk, pushes)
            hold
              back current
        miss
          save nothing, 0
  save reached, reaches-lists(start, walk)
  save out, make list
  walk current
    take q
    fork test, not(mentions-atom(q))
      hold
        push(out, q)
        turn next
    fork test, reached
      hold
        turn next
    save keep, true
    walk q/linear/terms/keys()
      take key
      fork test, and(and(is-state-atom(key), starts-with(key, <@>)), not(walk/local/has(key-root(key))))
        hold
          save keep, false
          halt
    fork test, keep
      hold
        push(out, q)
  back out

# ---- forgetting what a statement writes ----

form written-fields
  mark shared
  link names, like list, like text
  link fields, like list, like text
  link everything-written, like boolean

# WHAT A BODY WRITES, split by what it can change. A name written is forgotten whole. A FIELD written through a plain
# path changes that field of whatever record the path reaches, so every atom whose path passes through a field of that
# NAME goes, whatever its root. A write through a computed index or a list position may land anywhere, and every state
# atom goes
task forget-writes
  take current, like list, like inequality
  take start, like list, like node-handle
  like list, like inequality

  save found
    make written-fields
      bind names, texts()
      bind fields, texts()
      bind everything-written, false
  walk start
    take one
    visit-writes(one, found)
  fork test, found/everything-written
    hold
      back without-state(forget(current, found/names))
  back drop-fields(forget(current, found/names), found/fields)

task visit-writes
  take handle, like node-handle
  take found, like written-fields
  mark private

  fork test, found/everything-written
    hold
      back
  sift handle
    case statement-handle
      sift node
        case assign
          link target
          sift target
            case variable
              link target-name
              push(found/names, target-name)
            case member
              link member-target
              link member-name
              save plain, false
              sift plain-path(target)
                case some
                  link path
                  save plain, true
                case none
                  save nothing, 0
              fork test, and(and(not(has-index(target)), not(digits-only(member-name))), plain)
                hold
                  push(found/fields, member-name)
                miss
                  save found/everything-written, true
            miss
              save found/everything-written, true
        case let
          link let-name
          push(found/names, let-name)
        case for-each
          link item
          push(found/names, item)
          sift for-each-index(node)
            case some
              link index-name
              push(found/names, index-name)
            case none
              save nothing, 0
        case function
          link task-name
          link fn-params
          walk fn-params
            take param
            push(found/names, param/name)
        case guard
          link guard-body
          link handler
          sift handler
            case some
              link clause
              push(found/names, clause/name)
            case none
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
    case expression-handle
      sift node
        case closure
          link closure-params
          walk closure-params
            take param
            push(found/names, param/name)
        miss
          save nothing, 0
    miss
      save nothing, 0
  walk node-children(handle, skip-plain())
    take child
    visit-writes(child, found)

# a for-each's index name, when it has one, as the original's `typeof record.index === 'string'` asked
bind for-each-index-text
  take s, like statement
  like text
  case node
    text <(typeof ($s as any).index === 'string' ? ($s as any).index : '\\u0001')>
  case browser
    text <(typeof ($s as any).index === 'string' ? ($s as any).index : '\\u0001')>
  case rust
    text <String::new()>
  case swift
    text <"">
  case kotlin
    text <"">

task for-each-index
  take s, like statement
  like maybe, like text
  mark private

  save name, for-each-index-text(s)
  fork test, is-equal(name, <\\u0001>)
    hold
      back make none
  back make(some, name)

# ---- the closures an expression builds ----

# the closures an expression builds, in the order the original met them, nested ones excepted: a closure's own body
# reaches those
task closures-in
  take expression, like expression
  like list, like expression

  save out, make list
  save stack, handles()
  push(stack, expression-handle-of(expression))
  save seen, fresh-seen()
  walk test
    hook test, is-above(stack/length, 0)
    hook hold
      save handle, stack/pop()
      fork test, not(seen-first(seen, handle))
        hold
          turn next
      sift handle
        case expression-handle
          sift node
            case closure
              push(out, node)
              turn next
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
      walk node-children(handle, skip-places())
        take child
        push(stack, child)
  back out

# ---- direction ----

# how a body moves a name: `up` when every write is an increment by a constant >= 0, `down` for decrements, `any`
# otherwise (a rebinding, a computed step, a write inside a closure, a member write)
task direction-of
  take state, like hold-state
  take calls, like hold-calls
  take name, like text
  take body, like list, like statement
  like text

  save ups, 0
  save downs, 0
  save stack, block-handles(body)
  save seen, fresh-seen()
  walk test
    hook test, is-above(stack/length, 0)
    hook hold
      save handle, stack/pop()
      fork test, not(seen-first(seen, handle))
        hold
          turn next
      sift handle
        case statement-handle
          save s, node
          sift s
            case function
              link task-name
              link fn-params
              link fn-body
              fork test, has-text(written-in-block(fn-body), name)
                hold
                  back <any>
              turn next
            case let
              link let-name
              fork test, is-equal(let-name, name)
                hold
                  back <any>
            case for-each
              link item
              fork test, is-equal(item, name)
                hold
                  back <any>
              sift for-each-index(s)
                case some
                  link index-name
                  fork test, is-equal(index-name, name)
                    hold
                      back <any>
                case none
                  save nothing, 0
            case assign
              link target
              save hit, false
              sift root-of(target)
                case some
                  link root
                  save hit, is-equal(root, name)
                case none
                  save hit, true
              fork test, hit
                hold
                  save is-variable, false
                  sift target
                    case variable
                      save is-variable, true
                    miss
                      save nothing, 0
                  sift step-of(state, calls, name, s)
                    case some
                      link step
                      fork test, not(is-variable)
                        hold
                          back <any>
                      fork test, is-minimum(step, 0.0)
                        hold
                          save ups, add(ups, 1)
                        miss
                          save downs, add(downs, 1)
                    case none
                      back <any>
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        case expression-handle
          sift node
            case closure
              link closure-params
              link closure-body
              fork test, has-text(written-in-block(closure-body), name)
                hold
                  back <any>
              turn next
            miss
              save nothing, 0
        miss
          save nothing, 0
      walk node-children(handle, skip-plain())
        take child
        push(stack, child)
  fork test, is-equal(downs, 0)
    hold
      back <up>
  fork test, is-equal(ups, 0)
    hold
      back <down>
  back <any>

# the constant an assignment adds to a name (`x = x + 2` is 2, `x -= 1` is -1), or none when it is not one
task step-of
  take state, like hold-state
  take calls, like hold-calls
  take name, like text
  take statement, like statement
  like maybe, like float

  sift statement
    case assign
      link target
      link op
      link value
      save side, make list
      sift to-linear(state, calls, value, side)
        case some
          link v
          fork test, is-above(side/length, 0)
            hold
              back make none
          sift op
            case set
              save own, 0.0
              fork test, v/terms/has(name)
                hold
                  save own, v/terms/get(name)
              fork test, or(is-unequal(own, 1.0), is-unequal(v/terms/keys()/length, 1))
                hold
                  back make none
              save constant, v/constant
              back make(some, constant)
            case add
              fork test, is-unequal(v/terms/keys()/length, 0)
                hold
                  back make none
              save constant, v/constant
              back make(some, constant)
            case subtract
              fork test, is-unequal(v/terms/keys()/length, 0)
                hold
                  back make none
              save constant, multiply(-1.0, v/constant)
              back make(some, constant)
            miss
              back make none
        case none
          back make none
    miss
      back make none
